<title>USA: CBOE to list six options on Jan 31, one on Feb 4.</title>
<headline>CBOE to list six options on Jan 31, one on Feb 4.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Board Options Exchange (CBOE) said Wednesday it would list options on six stocks on January 31 and on one other stock on February 4.</p>
<p>The following table lists the underlying stock's ticker symbol, the option's strike prices, exercise months and trading crowd or designated primary market maker (DPM).</p>
<p>The following six options will begin trading on January 31:</p>
<p>Ticker	 Strikes	   Exercises   Crowd/DPM</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>	15, 17-1/2,     Feb, Mar,   Xilinx Inc crowd</p>
<p>		 20		  Apr, Jul</p>
<p>	 25, 30, 35	Feb, Mar,   Bristol-Myers crowd</p>
<p>				     Apr, Jul</p>
<p>	55, 60, 65	Feb, Mar,   Hewlett-Packard crowd</p>
<p>				     May, Aug</p>
<p>	30, 35, 40	Feb, Mar,   O.T.A. Ltd</p>
<p>				     Apr, Jul</p>
<p>     10, 12-1/2,     Feb, Mar,   Option Funding Group</p>
<p>		 15		  Jun, Sep</p>
<p>     10, 12-1/2,     Feb, Mar,   Felt Trading</p>
<p>		 15		  Jun, Sep</p>
<p>The following option will begin trading on February 4:</p>
<p>Ticker	 Strikes	   Exercises   Crowd/DPM</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>     7-1/2, 10,	Feb, Mar,   Option Resource Group</p>
<p>		 12-1/2	    May, Aug</p>
<p>((--Derivatives desk, 312 408 8750)) ((E-mail: derivatives@reuters.com))</p>
